{{about|the game mechanic|the support gem|Additional Accuracy Support}}
'''Accuracy''' is a property of [[attack]] [[hit]]s. Together with the target's [[evasion]], it is used to calculate an attack's chance to hit. [[Spells]] do not benefit from accuracy, as they cannot be evaded. 

Accuracy can be gained from various sources, such as [[equipment]], [[buffs]], [[passive]]s, and [[skill]]s. Player characters inherently gain 2 base accuracy per [[level]], and 2 base accuracy for each point of [[dexterity]]. 

==Mechanics==
Accuracy is compared against the target's [[evasion]] to determine whether an attack hits or misses according to:<ref name="MaliceMechanics"/><ref name="cite3"/>

{{math|formula=
\text{Uncapped Chance to Hit} = {1.25* \text{Attacker's Accuracy} \over \text{Attacker's Accuracy} + (\text{Defender's Evasion} *  \frac{1}{5}) ^ {0.9} }
}}

{{math|formula=\text{Chance to Hit} = \min\left(\max\left(\text{Uncapped Chance to Hit}, .05\right), 1\right)
}}

Chance to hit can not be lower than 5%. It can be a maximum of 100%; there is no purpose in trying to exceed 100%.

* Effects that state {{c|mod|Can't be Evaded}} or {{c|mod|Always Hit}} (e.g. [[Resolute Technique]], [[Worthy Foe]]) will raise the chance to hit to 100%, ignoring all accuracy and evasion stats of the attacker and defender respectively.
* {{c|mod|Cannot Evade}} (e.g. [[Unwavering Stance]]) does the same, in reverse; all attacks against the subject will hit regardless of accuracy. 

[[Area of effect]] hits from attacks use accuracy in the same way as non-aoe hits; they can be evaded even when monsters are visibly inside an AoE.

In addition to its role in hitting, accuracy is checked a second time when attack hits attempt to deal a [[critical strike]]. Failing this accuracy check will cause a hit with sufficient critical strike chance to become a regular hit. This does not affect critical strikes by [[spell]]s.<ref name="cite4"/>

Stats that scale from accuracy, such as {{il|Obscurantis}} or {{il|Oskarm}}, reference the accuracy of the skill, not the accuracy of a specific hit. This means conditional accuracy stats do not affect them (e.g. {{c|mod|against Marked Enemy, against Unique Enemies, at Close Range}}). 

Base monster evasion rating depends on [[monster level]]. The below formula ignores bonuses from monster type or modifiers.

{{Math|formula = \text{Evasion} = (50 + 16 * \text{Level} ) * 1.0212^\text{Level}
}}

[[Minion]]s' [[attack]] hits inherently always hit. Minions do still have an accuracy rating, but is only used for conditional stats (e.g. {{il|Animate Guardian}} with {{il|Oskarm}}) and otherwise has no functional effects.

